### High-Severity Findings

#### 1. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org — *Assertion Roulette* family / *Unknown Test*
**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113–119)
**Risk:** This test always passes as long as no exception is thrown. A broken `Insert` that silently corrupts data will never be caught.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

#### 2. Conditional Test Logic

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org — *Conditional Test Logic*
**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 96–109)
**Risk:** One branch is never exercised (a `User` inserted as a plain `User` will never be a `PremiumUser`), so the `DiscountRate` assertion is dead code. The test gives false confidence about polymorphism handling.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — branching assertion
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Write two separate tests, each with a deterministic path:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### Medium-Severity Finding

#### 3. Sleepy Test

**Taxonomy:** testsmells.org — *Sleepy Test*
**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)
**Integration calibration:** Even for integration tests, a hard-coded `Thread.Sleep(3000)` is non-deterministic. It slows the suite and can flake under CI load. Downgraded from High → **Medium** because the test is explicitly integration-scoped.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — wall-clock sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout instead:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

